<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-ANGOLA AND CAMEROON DRAW 1-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ANGOLA AND CAMEROON DRAW 1-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Angola and Cameroon drew 1-1</p>
<p>(halftime 0-0) in their World Cup African zone group four</p>
<p>qualifier in Luanda on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Angola - Akwa (55th min)</p>
<p>Cameroon - Patrick Mboma (54th min)]</p>
<p>Attendance: 60,000</p>
<p>    Standings    P  W  D  L  F  A  Pts</p>
<p> Cameroon	  5  3  2  0  8  3  11</p>
<p> Angola	    5  2  3  0  6  3   9</p>
<p> Zimbabwe	  4  1  1  2  4  3   4</p>
<p> Togo		4  0  0  4  3 12   0</p>
<p>    Remaining matches: June 8 Togo v Zimbabwe, Aug 17	Togo</p>
<p>v Angola, Zimbabwe v Cameroon</p>
</text>
